### LCD Panel

The actual display will show only the applicable items.
<PIC:Manual10_3>
{{image description: LCD panel information diagram labeling shutter speed, busy status, ISO speed, white balance icons, drive mode, AF mode, metering mode, shots remaining, aperture, battery check, flash exposure compensation, and CF card warning status.}}

Select the item to be set.

Turn the dial to select the menu item, then press <SET>

<PIC:Manual10_85>
{{image description: Parameters screen for Set 1 with Sharpness highlighted. Slider rows show Contrast, Sharpness, Saturation, and Color tone, with scale marks and MENU at the lower right.}}

<PIC:Manual10_86>
{{image description: Parameter effect table with columns Parameter, Minus, and Plus. It lists Contrast low contrast to high contrast, Sharpness less sharp outline to sharp outline, Saturation low saturation to high saturation, and Color tone reddish skin tone to yellowish skin tone.}}

Set the desired setting.

Turn the dial to select the desired effect, then press <SET>. Press the <MENU> button to return to the menu.

<PIC:Manual10_87>
{{image description: Parameters screen for Set 1 with Sharpness selected and the adjustment marker shifted toward the plus side of the slider.}}

Set the Quick Control Dial switch to enabled and, while looking at the viewfinder or LCD panel, turn the Quick Control Dial. Turn the Quick Control Dial while pressing the shutter button halfway or within the metering timer after pressing the shutter button halfway.

<PIC:Manual10_138>
{{image description: Rear camera control drawing with an arrow indicating rotation of the quick control dial near the SET button.}}

